/*!
    \previouspage {Changes in Previous Versions}
    \page qtul-changes.html
    \title What's New in 2.12
    \brief Changes in v2.12.0

    \QUL maintains source compatibility between minor releases.
    However, some changes may require you to adapt the application code
    accordingly. The following sections highlight such changes:

    \section1 New features
    \list
        \li Added support for the following target platforms:
        \list
          \li Tier-1 support for
              \l{Infineon TRAVEO T2G}{TRAVEO T2G 6M DDR Evaluation Kit}.
          \li Tier-2 support for
              \l{Infineon PSOC Edge E84 Evaluation Kit}{Infineon \tm{PSOC} Edge E84 evaluation kit}.
          \li Tier-3 support for \c{NXP RW612 on Zephyr} and \c{Renesas RA8P1}.

        \endlist
        \li Added DeviceLink support to Infineon TRAVEO T2G targets built
            using either the Green Hills or IAR toolchains. This enables
            automated UI testing using Squish.
        \li QmlProject improvements or updates:
        \list
        \li Parse translation data in all the \c qmlproject files before
            generating a list of languages.
        \li Added the \l MCU.Config.translationStorageSection property to
            enable defining a separate storage section for translation files.
        \li Added the \l{MCU.Config.glyphsLayoutCacheSize} property to define
            the cache size for the glyph layout and shaping data.
        \li Added the \l{--generate-resource-binaries} command-line option to
            enable regeneration of resource binaries only without exporting
            any configuration, QML files, and source files.
        \li Keep the font file for the Monotype Spark font engine in the
            resource binary, enabling version and checksum verification.
        \li The list of languages supported by the application is based
            on the translation files in the main QmlProject file.
        \li Added the following MCU.Config properties to support the Safe Renderer module:
        \list
            \li \l{MCU.Config.safeTextCachePolicy} to enable defining
            cache policy for dynamic \l SafeText resources.
            \li \l{MCU.Config.safeBitmapRuntimeAllocationType} to define the
                memory allocation type for accessing the SafeImage, SafePicture,
                and static SafeText resources.
            \li \l{MCU.Config.safeBitmapStorageSection} to enable defining a
                memory section for \l SafeText, \l SafeImage, and \l SafePicture.
            \li \l{MCU.Config.safeRendererCrcAlgorithm} to define a CRC algorithm
                for Qt Safe Layout tool.
            \li \l{MCU.Config.safeTextFontDirectory} to configure the fonts directory.
            \li \l{MCU.Config.safeTextRuntimeAllocationType} to define a memory
                allocation type for the dynamic SafeText resources.
            \li \l{MCU.Config.safeTextStorageSection} to define a memory
                section to store the dynamic SafeText resources.
        \endlist
        \endlist
        \li Removed the GCC compiler-specific options and flags from
            \c CompilerExtraOptions, as these options and flags were also set
            in the CMake toolchain file (\c armgcc.cmake). This avoids hard-coding
            the options and flags, so that they are customizable.
        \li Added \l{Qul::activeLanguages} property to get the list of
            languages that the application supports.
        \li Added \l date value type to enable support for \l{Position::}{timestamp}
            instance in \l Position instances.
        \li Added \l{Qul::validateMonotypeDataTableChecksums}() to verify the
            integrity of Monotype data tables stored in external flash. Storing
            these data tables in an external flash saves approximately \c ~57 KB
            on the internal flash. Refer to
            \l{Placing Monotype data tables in external flash} for more
            information.
        \li Updated the \l{thermo} demo to store the Monotype data tables in QSPI
            by default on \c{STM32F769I Discovery Kit}.
        \li Added \l{Qul::initResources}() options to enable control the
            initialization behavior.
        \li Added \l{MCU.Config.glyphsLayoutCacheSize} to control the size of
            cache for glyph layout data.
        \li \c qmltocpp improvements:
        \list
        \li Improved code that sets all the property bindings for a given root
            object to use table-based setters, which reduces code footprint
            significantly.
        \li Added error checks for built-in read-only list property.
        \endlist
        \li Added support for \l{Coco} to get code coverage results from the
            target hardware.
        \li Added support to independently update application and its resource
            data. Also added \l{Qul::}{queryResourceStorageSectionInfo}()
            and more options to \l{Qul::}{initResources}() API, which enables UI
            features based on what resource data is available for OTA (Over The Air)
            updates.
        \li RTOS, SDK and compiler upgrades:
        \list
        \li MSVC compiler to 2022 on Windows 11.
        \li Renesas RH850/D1M1A RGL SDK to v2.2.0a.
        \li Renesas platform SDK to version 25.06.00.
        \li NXP platform SDK to version 25.09.00.
        \li STM32CubeH7 SDK to version 1.12.1.
        \li Zephyr RTOS to v4.1.
        \endlist
        \li Improved cache memory usage reports in the performance logs,
            counting all the allocated space including block overhead.
        \li Added \l{Qul::SharedImage::}{maybeTexture}() method to check if
            there is enough space in the resource cache, instead of asserting.
        \li Added multi-line elide mode, which you can enable using the
            \l{MCU.Config.Experimental.multiLineElide} QmlProject property. This
            mode elides any line that exceeds the available width. It does not
            require an explicit height to be set.
        \li Added \l{Text::}{maximumLineCount} property to limit the number of
            visible lines in a \l Text item.
        \li Improved navigation API:
        \list
         \li Added \l CoordinateAnimation to animate the transition
             between two coordinates.
         \li Optimized memory requirements for \l geoCoordinate.
         \li Added the \l QtPositioning global type, which offers the \l[QtPositioning]{QtPositioning::}{coordinate}() method.
         \li Added \l{geoCoordinate::}{distanceTo}() method to
             calculate distance in meters between the two coordinates.
         \li Added \l{Qul::GeoPositionInfo::}{speed} and
             \l{Qul::GeoPositionInfo::}{timestamp} to enable applications to
             configure these properties in a \l{Qul::}{GeoPositionInfo}. The
             corresponding read-only properties that enable you access these
             properties in QML are \l{Position::speed} and
             \l{Position::timestamp}.
        \endlist

    \endlist

    \section1 Fixed issues
    \section2 \QULPackage v2.12.1
    \list
        \li Removed the \c -ffreestanding compiler flag from the ARMGCC
            toolchain file. This avoids using the incompatible
            \c <cmath> header while building with GCC 13 or later versions.
        \li Fixed \l{Qt Quick Ultralite Automotive Cluster Demo}{automotive} and
            \l{Qt Quick Ultralite Motorcycle Cluster Demo}{motor_cluster} demos to
            avoid a crash on Windows 10 with MSVC 2019. Moved the task and timer
            handling to \c std::map and \c std::vector to avoid loosing any data
            while the task is still active.
        \li Removed \c bytesPerLine and updated
            \l{Qul::PlatformInterface::ImageDecoder::}{imageInformation} to
            include all properties of an image.
        \li Upgrades:
        \list
        \li Fixed CVE-2024-0151 vulnerability by upgrading the ARM GNU toolchain
            headers to v15.2.rel1.
        \li Upgraded TRAVEO T2G CYT4DN's ModusToolbox \c tviic2d-gfx-mw driver
            to version 1.0.1.
        \endlist
        \li \c qmltocpp fixes:
        \list
        \li Fix crash while parsing Connections that handle a signal with parameters.
        \li Fix regression in properties of type \c{ListModel<T>}.
        \li Parse extra properties of an Item while resolving property bindings.
        \li Update visibility of child items when their parent
            Item's visibility changes.
        \li Check directory imports to include only relevant QML Component
            definitions that the current Component depends on. If there is no
            dependency on any Component in the directory, ignore the import.
        \endlist
        \li Added support for the native Infineon resource generator tool on Linux for
            TRAVEO T2G 6M Lite.
        \li Fixed the layout logic for Item type to handle changes to its implicit size.
        \li Updated \c qmlprojectexporter to also consider \c translationStorageSection
            defined in the board defaults CMake configuration.
    \endlist
    \section2 \QULPackage v2.12.0
    \list
        \li Enabled TRAVEO T2G targets to use the resource cache to preserve
            assets for multiple frames when using OTF layers. This avoids visual
            artifacts on the OTF layer when the texture data it's rendering gets
            invalidated in \QUL Core.
        \li Fixed out of memory exception on
            \l{STM32F769I Discovery Kit}{STM32F769I} target based on IAR toolchain.
            Changed to a fixed stack of size 24K for IAR builds too.
        \li Fixed graphical glitches when drawing path strokes on T2G TRAVEO boards.
        \li Fixed the JPEG decoder to allocate memory dynamically instead of using a
            hard coded memory address on TRAVEO T2G targets.
        \li Fixed incorrect perspective transforms on TRAVEO T2G targets when
            \c{destRect.topLeft() != srcRect.topLeft()}.
        \li Improved error reporting when surface allocation fails on TRAVEO T2G.
        \li Fixed text caching to avoid visual artifacts because of removed
            entries when the drawing engine is still reading them asynchronously.
        \li Fixed platform adaptation for Renesas RH850 to use CPU fallback engine
            for RGB332 pixel format.
        \li \c qmltocpp fixes:
        \list
         \li Fix code generated for component layout with many items.
         \li Ignore \c import statements if a module is importing itself.
         \li Skip generating the translation function if no translation files
             are found.
        \endlist
        \li \c qmlprojectexporter fixes:
        \list
         \li Warnings related to C++ compiler options.
         \li Use correct URI for the Qt Safe Renderer module.
        \endlist
        \li Fixed \l{PositionSource::}{position} property to make sure it is
            accessible from QML.
        \li Fixed GHS compiler generated dependency file suffix information, to
            make sure Ninja knows the correct file name.
        \li Fixed a crash because of resetting a ListView or Repeater model from
            the delegate.
        \li Fixed \c fontcompiler warnings by disabling the char attribute
            mapping to the corresponding cluster value.
        \li Optimized text performance by avoiding unnecessary re-layout and
            clearing cache before rendering.
        \li Fixed memory corruption on TRAVEO T2G, where the JPEG decoder
            was allocating memory dynamically instead of using a hard coded
            memory address.
        \li Fixed text cache implementation to call \c waitUntilAsyncReadFinished()
            before removing entries from the cache.
    \endlist
    \section1 New APIs

    \section2 APIs for application development

    \sincelist Qt Quick Ultralite 2.12

    \section2 APIs for platform development

    \sincelist Qt Quick Ultralite (Platform) 2.12

    \section1 Changes in Previous Versions

